// empty-difference.csg — a `difference()` whose subtrahend CONTAINS the
// minuend, so the result is genuinely empty (a 10³ cube minus a 20³ cube).
//
// This is the regression pin for the empty-shape abort class: OCCT's
// `BRepMesh_IncrementalMesh_2` on a shape with NO sub-shapes does not throw,
// it aborts the whole WASM module with `wasmTable.get(...) is not a function`,
// which poisons the kernel singleton. A `.csg` that evaluates to nothing is
// reachable from real designs, so the importer must yield an empty model plus
// a warning rather than taking the host down.
//
// Expected: loads successfully with 0 solids and no crash.
group() {
  difference() {
    cube(size = [10, 10, 10], center = true);
    cube(size = [20, 20, 20], center = true);
  }
}
